# NAT-083 (this project): the etc/rc of the first APFS-root run.
# init has already run its own checks when it reads this file. The Darwin programs below are Apple's, taken unmodified from the iOS 16.5 root
# (dynamically linked: they run through /usr/lib/dyld and the shared cache), and their output is short, so that the kernel's log (head 8 KiB +
# tail 32 KiB come back) still holds the mount lines of the kernel, init's checks and the end of this file. Then process 1 becomes Apple's launchd
# (/sbin/launchd.darwin) with an EMPTY /redwood/LaunchDaemons: the question is whether launchd starts and stays, not what it would start.
/bin/df
/sbin/mount
/bin/ps -A
/usr/bin/vm_stat
exec /sbin/launchd.darwin
